hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2719","###\n Narrated to us by Abu Bishr al-Wasiti, who said: Narrated to us by Khalid, meaning Ibn Abdullah, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Tufayl, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas, \The Ramal (brisk walking with shoulders heaving) is done for three circuits around the House"
"2720","Nasr ibn Marzuq narrated to us: Asad narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us: from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Quraysh said: ""Muhammad and his companions have been weakened by the fever of Yathrib."" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived for the year he arrived, he said to his companions: ""Walk briskly around the House three times so that the polytheists may see your strength."" When they walked briskly, Quraysh said: ""They have not been weakened."""
